@scoped(['src/Controller/**', 'plugins/**/src/Controller/**'])
## CakePHP 5.4+ controllers and responses

- Prefer `#[RequestToDto]` for request→DTO mapping when introducing new typed request payloads.
- Use `JsonStreamResponse` for streamed JSON responses instead of buffering large payloads in memory.
@endscoped

@scoped(['src/Model/**', 'plugins/**/src/Model/**'])
## CakePHP 5.4+ ORM defaults and associations

- HasMany / BelongsToMany default strategy changed from `select` to `subquery`. Do not assume `select` unless the association or query explicitly sets it. Follow existing association strategy in sibling tables.
- Nested `associated` options may follow `contain()`-style nesting. Prefer the application's existing `patchEntity` / `save` association shape.
- Entity class-type checks apply on patch/save/delete/load — pass the expected entity type and do not rely on silent type coercion.
- Prefer `Connection::afterCommit()` for side effects that must run only after a successful commit.
@endscoped

@scoped(['src/Command/**', 'plugins/**/src/Command/**'])
## CakePHP 5.4+ commands (scoped)

- When editing existing commands, keep the file's established io/args pattern. For new commands, `$this->io` / `$this->args` are preferred.
@endscoped

@scoped(['tests/**'])
## CakePHP 5.4+ testing

- Prefer `TestCase::mockModel()` (Mockery) when mocking table classes in unit tests if the project already uses Mockery.
@endscoped

@scoped(['src/View/**', 'templates/**', 'plugins/**/templates/**'])
## CakePHP 5.4+ views and text

- Prefer `FormHelper::enumOptions()` when building select options from backed enums.
- Prefer `Text::mask()` for masking sensitive display strings.
@endscoped
{% endif %}
